# InsiderExperiment — Agent A findings (consolidated)

Repository **InsiderExperiment** at anchored SHA `12d9fd36cf055cb10ea67a3fc737e404217bc95a` (master, 2026-08-25).
Agent A, Direction A (the program closed hypotheses too early or too hard). Honest advocacy, not neutral review.

## The strongest case for the thesis in this repository

This repository closed a live hypothesis on a single second-moment figure — a minimum detectable effect of
49.35 bp per month against a BLOCKED bar of 40 — and then forbade its own reopening ("no amendment can
authorize Stage B", REGISTRATION.md:800). The arithmetic is sound: I reproduced all four series and the full
Newey-West grid to four decimals from the centered store. The case is about what the 49.35 was computed on and
compared against. The registered primary weighting (market capitalization) was never run; a median-dollar-volume
proxy was, and the closure attributes that proxy's concentration to "the registered primary". The registered
Stage B inference (Carhart residual) was never measured, although the residual dispersion is computable from the
centered store without ever producing the intercept the seal protects. The 30-to-40 bp band the BLOCKED bar sits
on top of carries no citation anywhere in the repository, while the closure sentence borrows "the range the
literature reports". And on the identical names the registered equal-weighted secondary came in at 34.29 —
inside DEGRADED — with promotion refused as "selecting a weighting scheme by its answer", a ground the
repository's own Section 0.1 contradicts, since a second moment is by its own definition not the answer.

Scratch work: `scratchpad/work/agentA/InsiderExperiment/recompute_mde.py` (+ `.out`) and `verify_tables.py` (+ `.out`).

